=== Parity notes ===
- Web source web/src/components/motion/FadeIn.tsx is a motion wrapper: fade + slide-up (opacity 0->1, y 12->0),
  optional delay, reduced-motion => initial=false (final state, no entry). It fetches nothing and renders no text.
- Native surface composes the tested motion atom (io.teslasync.android.components.motion.FadeIn), binds the device
  motion preference (P1/S8) via the atom's reduced-motion plumbing, emits the one-shot PII-safe view.opened
  diagnostic (P1/S11, slug=FadeIn), and tags the wrapper root so every state (incl. empty) is locatable.
- States reproduced: animated reveal (motion enabled), immediate final state (reduced motion), transparent empty
  wrapper. Generic data-surface states (loading/error/stale/offline) are intentionally absent and the rationale is
  documented in FadeInModel.kt: the only input is the always-available motion-preference signal; inventing async
  states would model a dependency the web spec does not have (covenant: no scope narrowing, no silent drift).
- i18n: the source renders no strings; the surface carries none (preview sample text is private, tooling-only).

